Secured and monitored web infrastructure

A user wants to access the website www.foobar.com from their browser.

The user types https://www.foobar.com. DNS resolves www.foobar.com to the load balancer IP address. The user sends an HTTPS request to the load balancer. The request passes through a firewall before reaching the load balancer. The load balancer distributes the traffic between two backend servers. Each server has a firewall, a web server, an application server, application files, a database, and a monitoring client.

